  title: "44 · Simple subsurface scattering"
  description: "A cheap translucency term added to Standard lighting in a custom lighting function: light passing through the object is approximated with pow(saturate(dot(viewDir, -(lightDir + normal * distortion))), concentration), scaled by (1 - thickness). The light rotates and is behind the objects for part of the cycle - that is when the effect shows. Left: plain Standard for comparison."
